 "root_cause": "Local market limits were applied after sorted(root.iterdir()) had enumerated the entire directory and Path.read_bytes had consumed the entire manifest. The scanner also lacked the existing descriptor reader identity/link checks. A nominal 64-entry/64-KiB boundary therefore did not bound actual enumeration/read work.",
 "changes": [
  "Enumerate via an explicitly closed native scandir iterator, retain at most 64 entries and reject upon observing entry 65 before scanning manifests",
  "Keep original sorted order and 32 valid candidates for sources within the declared entry limit",
  "Parameterize the existing descriptor reader with its original 1-MiB default and reuse it for 64-KiB market manifests",
  "Reject declared oversized files before content reads; cap actual reads at 65537 bytes and reuse regular-file/link-count and identity/size/mtime checks",
  "Skip invalid/changing/hardlinked manifests and preserve actual worker ownership after caller cancellation; no capture, plugin import, installation or authorization change"
 ],
